# Append-only files (AGENT_PROMPT.md section 17; engine/memory.py APPEND_ONLY, + the event calendar): when two
# runs add to the same file at the same time (hourly scan, daily research, Claude's Brain workflow), the `append`
# merge driver (append_merge.py) keeps BOTH additions, each one whole, one after the other. It replaced
# `merge=union`, which merges line by line and wrote the lines two additions share only once - on 26 Sep 2026 that
# interleaved two strategy cards in strategies_lab.yaml and broke both. The workflows register the driver before
# `git pull --rebase`; where it is not registered, git stops with a normal conflict (safe) instead.
# memory_guard.py still checks that no earlier line was changed or removed, and after the pull that each file still
# starts with the pushed main (memory_guard.py --after-sync).
